# Dining Hall Experience-Only (No Menus)

**Contract (authoritative):** `docs/guardrails/2026-08-15_dining-hall-experience-only-no-menus.md`  
**Clarified:** 2026-08-17 — menus are irrelevant; status reports do not need menu data

## Hard rule

**Menuply does not analyze dining-hall menus or menu items.** Dining halls exist so users can report **what is going on** (status) and **comment**. Menu data is not required.

## Never without explicit current-turn approval

- View Menu / Today’s Menu / CK / OCR / menu-item identity for `restaurant_type = dining_hall`
- Using menu data as a prerequisite for dining-hall status reports
- Treating dining halls as claimable restaurant businesses

## Allowed

- Status reports (wait, seating, sold-out, venue ops, busy, notes)
- Comments on the place / those reports
- Guest contribution under the guest open reporting contract

## Agent stop line

> This change would add dining-hall menu tracking, menu-item analysis, or a Today’s Menu / View Menu surface. I have not done that. Dining halls are status reports + comments only.

## Mandatory on EVERY task completion

End every response with:

> ☐ DINING HALL CERTIFICATION: Dining-hall menus [unchanged unused | user-approved menu work]; status+comments [unchanged | implemented].
